.README
Python Control Flow Lab – Drilling Well Readings

Project Overview

This project demonstrates the use of Python fundamentals and control flow to analyse drilling well pressure readings.

The program classifies pressure readings, converts pressure from PSI to kPa, filters valid active readings, and calculates average pressure for each well. 

Conclusion

This exercise demonstrates how Python control flow can be used to process drilling telemetry data, identify invalid observations, filter operational readings, and calculate well-level pressure averages.

The results provide a simple example of how programming can support data analysis in the oil and gas industry.